※ pl4g-test: compile=fail
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4341 LANG_NAME_THE_IMAGE_USES

※ A variable at the top level is known in the image by its name, so one named
※ as a function of the runtime is a second symbol of that name: a program
※ writing it would write over the runtime's code.  Refused where it is defined,
※ as a function of such a name is (`name-the-image-uses`).

let std := ⎕import("std")

let pl4g_args: mut u8 = 3u8

@[startup, impure]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    pl4g_args ← pl4g_args + 1u8
    if pl4g_args = 4u8: 0u6 else: 1u6
